Pinned Java re-review and corrections — 2026-11-14 UTC
User request: review again and ensure the changed behavior agrees with Java. Starting revision feb535cf; working tree was clean. Continued the Pull-dispatch scope of Plan 02/02a/02b; did not edit plans or expand any full-phase compatibility claim.

Reference: read matching Maven 5.5.1 client/remoting source jars from the local repository, especially DefaultMQPushConsumerImpl.pullMessage, PullAPIWrapper.pullKernelImpl, MQClientAPIImpl.pullMessage, and NettyRemotingAbstract.invoke0/scanResponseTable. The pinned client contract has ASYNC hand-off, 15000 ms suspend, 30000 ms RPC timeout, semaphore-based admission, and no four-task cap. Internal ownership/join implementation remains the existing approved Rust design.

Confirmed mismatches and changes:
1. Slave pulls cleared both the commit bit and the commitOffset value. Java clears only the bit. Corrected header preservation, and later retained nonpositive values too: Java memory-offset absence is -1 with commit disabled, whereas Rust previously emitted zero. Broadcasting still sends zero. Regression covers master/slave 42 and disabled commit values NotFound/-2/0.
2. Max-span flow control applied to orderly pulls. Java checks it only when the live consumeOrderly flag is false. Corrected the condition and moved count/size flow control ahead of orderly lock/offset work, as Java does. Regression verifies orderly skipping max-span, a live flag change restoring it, and count flow control remaining active.
3. A cold route lookup spent the 30-second Pull RPC deadline. Java refreshes routing before invoking pullMessage with the full timeout. Lookup now uses the runtime's configured route timeout; a fresh absolute 30-second Pull deadline is established at the RPC call. A paused-clock peer delaying route lookup 2 seconds and RPC response 30.5 seconds proves the async cleanup-grace mode still receives its full budget.
4. The first real Broker run failed before either probe: mqadmin topicStatus appends 'Topic Put TPS: 0.0', which the empty-topic parser treated as an offset. Queue parsing now requires numeric queue/min/max columns; the self-test includes the actual footer.

Red/green evidence: all three initial regressions failed against the starting production implementation (slave header 0 vs 42; route-refresh response wait expired; orderly span hit 50 ms flow control). The added disabled-commit regression independently failed with 0 vs -1. All pass after correction.

Pinned invocation oracle: new PushPullDispatchFixtures invokes actual DefaultMQPushConsumerImpl and PullAPIWrapper methods with offline recording subclasses, holds every callback, and verifies 80 distinct queue requests use ASYNC before any response. It verifies route refresh followed by a full 30000 ms timeout, 15000 ms suspend, slave commit-bit/value rules, missing memory offset, concurrent span delay and orderly cache rules. Maven verify drift-checks fixtures/consumer/push-pull-dispatch.json, consumed by the Rust regressions. No Broker, sockets or running Java services are used by this oracle; constructor-free recording subclasses follow existing fixture conventions.

