Additional test-only review fix: the earlier narrow push_pull_ run had one warm-route deadline failure even though the subsequent full 314-test consumer suite passed. The paused Tokio clock could auto-advance past the transport grace deadline while the OS socket response was still becoming readable. Replaced the peer sleeps with explicit virtual-time advances and retained a yielding clock-keeper task (owned by JoinSet) to prevent uncontrolled auto-advances during I/O. This preserves the late-response and cold-route regressions without lengthening deadlines or changing production code. Repeated the 7 focused push_pull_ tests ten times; all ten runs passed. Strict workspace Clippy passed again. Live evidence at 6d6db7ed remains the exact final production code; this later commit changes test scheduling only.
